      {
        "id": 218023,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-05-09T01:54:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>These sure do get asked a lot.&nbsp; Per Dave, whoever created the boost/hinder decides when it applies.&nbsp; Each applies to a single effect die.&nbsp; So if Bunker had two non-exclusive boosts (that he created), he could apply them to the same die, to different dice, or could save either or both of them.&nbsp; Whoever created the hinder decided which die it applies to.&nbsp; Also, they don't change which is min/mid/max if you were wondering.</p><p>It occurs to me to wonder when these decisions are made, though.&nbsp; Can someone decide not to bother applying a hinder to you after you've decided to use a boost?&nbsp; Can you choose to save a boost until after you find out if a hinder is being applied?&nbsp; Presumably it's assumed the heroes agree on what boosts should be used on any given roll, but what if they don't?</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:50:02.902Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 3,
        "readers_count": 2,
        "score": 0.6,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 18026,
        "topic_slug": "boosts-and-hinders",
