        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>These sure do get asked a lot.&nbsp; Per Dave, whoever created the boost/hinder decides when it applies.&nbsp; Each applies to a single effect die.&nbsp; So if Bunker had two non-exclusive boosts (that he created), he could apply them to the same die, to different dice, or could save either or both of them.&nbsp; Whoever created the hinder decided which die it applies to.&nbsp; Also, they don&#39;t change which is min/mid/max if you were wondering.</p><p>It occurs to me to wonder when these decisions are made, though.&nbsp; Can someone decide not to bother applying a hinder to you after you&#39;ve decided to use a boost?&nbsp; Can you choose to save a boost until after you find out if a hinder is being applied?&nbsp; Presumably it&#39;s assumed the heroes agree on what boosts should be used on any given roll, but what if they don&#39;t?</p>",
